{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfggr8KhowwZovn4ba6gs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G2iWDKqBj8JszuXfg6NWx3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_3\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built` (tally span judged against a personal expected span, switching judged by closeness to a personal ideal switching rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, a personal left/right lean). The one change: people weigh the end of a sequence more than its middle — the last flips they read leave the strongest impression, and a sequence that ends on a repeat (the last two flips the same) reads as a streak just starting, while one that ends on a switch reads as still random — so a shared reward on ending with a switch is added. Of two sequences with the same number of switches, people pick the one whose final two flips differ more often than the incumbent predicts, addressing the critique that the incumbent is blind to where the switches fall.\nEOF\necho ending_switch_recency_rule_built > $D/model_name.txt\nsed -e 's/^\"\"\"Person-specific ideal switching rate in the rule-built tally\\/switch\\/triplet judgement./\"\"\"Recency of the final transition added to the person-specific switching-ideal model./' \\\n    -e 's/^pairs that differ mainly in switching.$/pairs that differ mainly in switching. Added change: a shared reward on a\\nsequence ending with a switch (its last two flips differ) rather than a repeat,\\nbecause the end of a sequence leaves the strongest impression./' \\\n    -e 's/^        \"log_len\": float(np.log(len(a) \\/ 6.0)),/        \"log_len\": float(np.log(len(a) \\/ 6.0)),\\n        \"end_sw_diff\": float(a[-1] != a[-2]) - float(b[-1] != b[-2]),/' \\\n    -e 's/^    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))/&\\n    end_sw_diff = pm.Data(\"end_sw_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))/' \\\n    -e 's/^    # Person-specific left\\/right response bias/    # Shared reward on ending with a switch (recency of the final transition).\\n    delta = pm.Normal(\"delta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\\n\\n&/' \\\n    -e 's/^        + side\\[participant_id\\]$/        + delta * end_sw_diff\\n&/' \\\n    /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built.py > $D/candidate.py\ngrep -n \"end_sw\\|delta\\|Added\" $D/candidate.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3089,"cache_read_input_tokens":82782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3089,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e39b4f3a-afdb-41fb-88f6-919c1b6e91b6","uuid":"fb07774e-8235-4d56-a9da-eec9992681da","timestamp":"2026-10-04T06:01:20.954Z","request_id":"req_011Cfggr7x8ctsdBdhNPgjJM"}
